```

### How do you exclude an auto-configuration class?

Sometimes auto-configuration creates beans you do not want. You can exclude specific classes using the `exclude` attribute on `@SpringBootApplication` or via a property in `application.yml`.

```java
package com.bank;

import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.security.servlet.SecurityAutoConfiguration;

// Exclude security auto-config during early development
@SpringBootApplication(exclude = SecurityAutoConfiguration.class)
public class NationalBankApplication {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(NationalBankApplication.class, args);
    }
}
```

```yaml
# Alternative: exclude via properties
spring:
  autoconfigure:
    exclude:
      - org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.security.servlet.SecurityAutoConfiguration
```

### What are common mistakes with layered architecture?

The most common mistake is injecting a Repository directly into a Controller, bypassing the Service layer. This looks harmless for simple reads but breaks down when business logic grows.

```java
// WRONG: Controller depends directly on Repository
@RestController
public class BadTransferController {

    @Autowired
    private AccountRepository accountRepository;

    @PostMapping("/api/v1/transfer")
    public ResponseEntity<String> transfer(@RequestBody TransferRequest req) {
        Account from = accountRepository.findById(req.fromId()).orElseThrow();
        Account to = accountRepository.findById(req.toId()).orElseThrow();
        // Business logic scattered in controller. No @Transactional.
        // If debit succeeds but credit fails, money disappears.
        from.setBalance(from.getBalance().subtract(req.amount()));
        to.setBalance(to.getBalance().add(req.amount()));
        accountRepository.save(from);
        accountRepository.save(to);
        return ResponseEntity.ok("Done");
    }
}
```

```java
// CORRECT: Controller delegates to Service with @Transactional
@RestController
public class GoodTransferController {

    private final TransferService transferService;

    public GoodTransferController(TransferService transferService) {
        this.transferService = transferService;
    }

    @PostMapping("/api/v1/transfer")
    public ResponseEntity<String> transfer(@RequestBody TransferRequest req) {
        transferService.execute(req.fromId(), req.toId(), req.amount());
        return ResponseEntity.ok("Transfer complete");
    }
}
```

### How does each layer get tested independently?

The layering enables the test pyramid. Each layer uses a different Spring test slice.

| Layer | Test Annotation | What Is Real | What Is Mocked | Speed |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Controller | `@WebMvcTest` | MockMvc, Jackson, Validators | Service (via `@MockBean`) | Fast |
| Service | No Spring (Mockito) | Service class | Repository (via `@Mock`) | Very fast |
| Repository | `@DataJpaTest` | JPA, EntityManager, DB | Nothing | Medium |
| Full stack | `@SpringBootTest` | Everything | Nothing | Slow |

```java
package com.bank.controller;

import com.bank.service.AccountService;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.springframework.beans.factory.annotation.Autowired;
import org.springframework.boot.test.autoconfigure.web.servlet.WebMvcTest;
import org.springframework.boot.test.mock.bean.MockBean;
import org.springframework.test.web.servlet.MockMvc;
import java.math.BigDecimal;

import static org.mockito.Mockito.when;
import static org.springframework.test.web.servlet.request.MockMvcRequestBuilders.get;
import static org.springframework.test.web.servlet.result.MockMvcResultMatchers.*;

@WebMvcTest(AccountController.class)
class AccountControllerTest {

    @Autowired
    private MockMvc mvc;

    @MockBean
    private AccountService accountService;

    @Test
    void returnsBalanceForValidAccount() throws Exception {
        when(accountService.getBalance("SAV2001"))
            .thenReturn(new BigDecimal("250000.00"));

        mvc.perform(get("/api/v1/accounts/SAV2001/balance"))
           .andExpect(status().isOk())
           .andExpect(content().string("250000.00"));
    }
}
```

